# Line endings are pinned to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# WHY, specifically. This machine has `core.autocrlf=true` globally, so without
# this file every checkout would rewrite the tree to CRLF. That is not a
# cosmetic worry here: a 2026-08-25 audit found three source files had drifted
# to CRLF while the other thirty-two were LF, and its finding was that a
# diff-based review of those files could no longer be scoped to the actual
# edits — every line reads as changed. The files were normalized by hand; this
# file is what stops the next checkout from undoing that.
#
# `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is the part that matters: `text=auto` alone
# normalizes what is STORED and still lets autocrlf convert what is CHECKED OUT.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Artifacts that must survive byte-for-byte. `events.jsonl` fixtures are real
# captured run streams replayed through the strict fold; rewriting their line
# endings would change what is being replayed.
*.jsonl -text
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
